Build Specification — App 17: STAG Schema Library
Completeness status: COMPLETE. All sections delivered in one pass. No truncation. Formatted for copy-paste into another conversation window. No tables, no boxes.

What It Is
A versioned package that contains the STAG schemas and rules. It packages the JSON Schema, the SHACL schema, the thirty-two semantic rules, and the codebook, in Python, R, and JavaScript, with versioned releases. It takes in nothing; it is a dependency. It puts out importable schema and rule modules. It is for developers building on STAG.

Core Requirements
Functional requirements:

Package the STAG JSON Schema (Artifact 2, Appendix B.1) as a versioned artifact.

Package the STAG SHACL schema (Artifact 2, Appendix B.3) as a versioned artifact.

Package the thirty-two semantic rules (Artifact 2, Appendix B.2) as a versioned artifact.

Package the STAG codebook (Artifact 2, Appendices A.1 through A.11) as a versioned artifact.

Provide the schemas and rules in three language bindings: Python, R, and JavaScript.

Provide a consistent API across the three bindings.

Support versioned releases, so a downstream consumer can pin a specific schema version.

Support the selection of a schema version at runtime.

Provide the rule engine as a callable library.

Provide the JSON Schema as a file and as an in-memory object.

Provide the SHACL schema as a file and as an in-memory object.

Provide the codebook as a file and as an in-memory object.

Provide the permitted value sets for each field as machine-readable data.

Provide the field list as machine-readable data.

Provide the type information for each field as machine-readable data.

Provide a validation function that runs the thirty-two semantic rules against a STAG record.

Provide a version compatibility check between a STAG record and a schema version.

Non-functional requirements:

Deterministic: same inputs produce same outputs.

No network dependency at runtime.

Fast: validation of a typical record in under one second.

Versioned: each release has a semantic version.

Reproducible: the library records the schema version in every validation report.

Well-tested: the library has a test suite that covers all thirty-two rules.

Documented: the library has API documentation and a codebook reference.

Portable: the library works on Linux, macOS, and Windows.

Input Specification
The library has no runtime inputs of its own. It is a dependency that other apps import.

For validation, the library takes:

Input 1. STAG record. Required. A JSON object conforming to the STAG schema.

Input 2. Schema version. Optional. The schema version to use. If not provided, the library uses the version pinned at import time.

Input 3. Strictness mode. Optional. Values: strict (all rules enforced, default), lenient (only structural rules enforced).

Input 4. Validation scope. Optional. Values: full (default), structural_only, semantic_only, shacl_only.

For version compatibility, the library takes:

Input 5. STAG record schema version. Required. The schema version declared in the record.

Input 6. Library schema version. Required. The schema version of the library.

Output Specification
For validation:

Output 1. Validation report. JSON. A pass or a list of violations. Each violation has a rule number, a rule name, a severity, a field path, an offending value, and a message.

Output 2. Pass indicator. Boolean. True if no violations.

Output 3. Schema version used. String.

Output 4. Rule set version used. String.

For version compatibility:

Output 5. Compatibility report. JSON. Whether the record's schema version is compatible with the library's schema version.

For data access:

Output 6. JSON Schema file. A string or a file path.

Output 7. SHACL schema file. A string or a file path.

Output 8. Codebook file. A string or a file path.

Output 9. Field list. JSON. The list of fields, with their types and permitted values.

Output 10. Rule list. JSON. The list of rules, with their numbers, names, and descriptions.

Output 11. Permitted value sets. JSON. For each field, the set of permitted values.

Module-by-Module Specification
Module 1: Schema Registry
Holds the STAG JSON Schema, the SHACL schema, and the codebook for each schema version. Provides lookup by version string. Provides a list of known versions. Provides the latest version.

Module 2: Rule Registry
Holds the thirty-two semantic rules for each schema version. Provides lookup by version string. Provides the rule list with numbers, names, and descriptions.

Module 3: Field Registry
Holds the field list for each schema version. Provides lookup by version string. Provides the type information and permitted value sets for each field.

Module 4: Validation Engine
Runs the thirty-two semantic rules against a STAG record. Uses the rule registry. Returns a validation report.

Module 5: JSON Schema Exporter
Provides the JSON Schema as a file and as an in-memory object.

Module 6: SHACL Schema Exporter
Provides the SHACL schema as a file and as an in-memory object.

Module 7: Codebook Exporter
Provides the codebook as a file and as an in-memory object.

Module 8: Version Compatibility Checker
Checks whether a record's schema version is compatible with the library's schema version. Returns a compatibility report.

Module 9: Python Binding
Provides the library API in Python. Uses jsonschema for JSON Schema validation. Uses pyshacl for SHACL validation. Uses rdflib for RDF handling.

Module 10: R Binding
Provides the library API in R. Uses jsonvalidate for JSON Schema validation. Uses rdflib for RDF handling. Uses a custom implementation for the semantic rules.

Module 11: JavaScript Binding
Provides the library API in JavaScript. Uses ajv for JSON Schema validation. Uses rdf-validate-shacl for SHACL validation. Uses n3 for RDF handling.

Module 12: Documentation Generator
Generates the API documentation from the source code and the codebook. Generates the codebook reference from the codebook data.

Module 13: Test Suite
Tests all thirty-two rules. Tests the JSON Schema. Tests the SHACL schema. Tests the version compatibility checker. Tests the field registry and the permitted value sets.

