6.2 The SHACL Schema
The SHACL schema is the graph schema for the STAG annotation record. It is written in SHACL Core, with SHACL-SPARQL for cross-node constraints. It has one SHACL shape per semantic rule that is expressible in SHACL. Each shape corresponds to one rule from Artifact 2, Appendix B.2.

The full SHACL shape file is deposited with the library.

6.3 The Semantic Rules
The semantic rules are the thirty-two rules from Artifact 2, Appendix B.2. Each rule is a pure function that takes a STAG record and returns pass or a violation. The rules are:

Rule 1. If intervention_classification is Non_definitional and cross_domain_counterfactual_dependence is Yes or No, then model_reference, counterfactual_intervention, counterfactual_description, counterfactual_result, material_change_test, material_change_result must be present.

Rule 2. Precedence as in Section 7.2 of Artifact 1.

Rule 3. If cross_domain_counterfactual_dependence is Yes, then intervention_source_domains together with intervention_target_domain must span at least two distinct declared domains.

Rule 4. If partition_kind is framework_level, then cross_domain_counterfactual_dependence must be Untestable and unclassified_reason must be inadmissible_partition.

Rule 5. If effective_description_change is Yes-strong and includes ΔAPP or ΔEFT, then external_justification must be populated.

Rule 6. All domain entries must belong to the partition identified by partition_registry_id and partition_version.

Rule 7. If derived_display_label is STAG-Discovered, partition_sensitivity is required; scale_separation must be recorded; ratio must be at or above the recorded minimum; scale_separation_source_kind must be external_value or external_coefficient; band_declared, band_min_ratio, and band_max_ratio must be populated; band_source must be populated, and band_source_citation must be populated when band_source is external_reference; and both independence_of_material_change_evidence and material_change_test_result_independence must be recorded. If derived_display_label is STAG-Definitional or any STAG-Intra variant, partition_sensitivity is required.

Rule 8. Node identity must be established from (S, M, G) alone, before any transition attribute is recorded and before any domain annotation is fixed.

Rule 9. Every annotation must declare tuple-matching rules, the M-equivalence rule, granularity, and the partition justification before node identity is finalized.

Rule 10. Supersession must be acyclic.

Rule 11. Every annotation must identify the theory, model, or scientific version under which it was produced.

Rule 12. If composition is composite, event_node must be populated and source_nodes must contain at least two entries.

Rule 13. If composition is not composite, event_node must be absent and transition attributes are stored on the edge. Self-loops carry regime_change.

Rule 14. validity_regime is an attribute and must not be consulted when determining node identity.

Rule 15. Regime attribute is required for every node. When the value is symmetric, broken, or crossover-band, order_parameter, control_parameter_point, phase_diagram_source, domain_specific_label, and framework_value_mapping must be populated. When the value is crossover-band, value_bands_if_crossover must be populated, regime_band_source must be populated and must be external_reference or analyst_chosen, with regime_band_analyst_chosen set true if analyst_chosen.

Rule 16. If two candidate descriptions share S, M, and G, node_identity must be merged. Under different partitions, the same pair is the same node; the domain annotation differs.

Rule 17. cross_domain_counterfactual_dependence = Not_tested is permitted only when intervention_classification = Not_applicable. An intervention performed with no result recorded is a validation error. An intervention performed with a result recorded but an uncertain material-change classification requires Uncertain.

Rule 18. If intervention_classification is Definitional or Definitional(expertise-dependent), cited_structural_result must be populated with result_reference, applicability_conditions, and conditions_check as a list of entries each having condition and condition_witness, at least one per applicability condition. Each condition_witness must name a specific equation, term, kernel, parameter range, or regime condition in the surviving description and must cite a source. A condition_witness naming only a general property is a validation error. If any applicability condition lacks a witness, entailment_basis must be E4 and intervention_classification must be Definitional(expertise-dependent). If a numerical result is cited in support of a Non_definitional classification, cited_numerical_result must be populated with citation, result_summary, classification_effect, and citation_scope.

Rule 19. If cross_domain_counterfactual_dependence is Intra_domain, intervention_source_domains must be a non-empty set contained within a single declared domain, intervention_target_domain must be that same domain, and cross_domain_intervention_available must be populated.

Rule 20. If either endpoint has regime_attribute.value = not_determinable, record regime_not_determinable = true and retain the derived label with the flag attached.

Rule 21. If derived_display_label is STAG-Unclassified, unclassified_reason must be populated and displayed with the label.

Rule 22. If a structural relation between two M's is recorded (integration_out or truncation), it must be recorded as a derived-from edge, not as an M-equivalence.

Rule 23. If effective_description_change is Yes-weak, derived_display_label must be STAG-Unclassified with unclassified_reason = weak_effective_description_basis.

Rule 24. If a merged decision is recorded on two descriptions with different Lagrangians, m_equivalence_basis and m_equivalence_witness must both be populated.

Rule 25. domain_mismatch is true if and only if intervention_target_domain is not a member of the set of domains to which the source and target nodes are assigned under the annotation's declared partition_id and partition_version.

Rule 26. If agreement_outcome is inconclusive for any core-tier field on which the derived label depends, the derived label is reported with provisional_flag = true attached.

Rule 27. If cross_domain_counterfactual_dependence is Intra_domain and the material-change classification is Uncertain, derived_display_label must be STAG-Unclassified with unclassified_reason = uncertain.

Rule 28. If material_change_test is a class change, material_change_test_justification must state the classification scheme.

Rule 29. evidential_anchoring_status is the field carrying the anchoring status of a STAG-Discovered annotation. For STAG-Discovered annotations: anchored if and only if all four anchoring conditions of Section 1.2 of Artifact 1 are satisfied; anchored_with_stated_limitations if all four are satisfied but at least one condition is flagged as interpretive or convention-dependent; preliminary if the case is used to develop or illustrate the codebook; candidate if the case is proposed as a possible instance. Operational determination: condition (a) requires cited_numerical_result.citation_scope = annotated_model or an annotator computation; condition (b) requires band_source = external_reference, band_source_citation populated, and band_min_ratio at or above the declared minimum; condition (c) requires independence_of_material_change_evidence = independent; condition (d) requires material_change_test_result_independence = independent.

Rule 30. For non-STAG-Discovered annotations, evidential_anchoring_status is not_applicable or not_assessed.

Rule 31. If defining_coupling_intervention = true, a second independent rater is required, and the case is excluded from STAG-Discovered unless the second rater independently confirms the intervention classification and the material-change result.

Rule 32. If agreement_outcome differs between the 0.5 and 0.7 thresholds, threshold_sensitive_flag must be true, and the falsification status of any dependent label must be reported as threshold-dependent.

Rule 33. If any field is marked not_determinable because a load-bearing source cannot be verified, the label is retained with the not_determinable flag attached and displayed alongside, and the flag is recorded in the annotation record under not_determinable_flag.

6.4 The Codebook
The codebook is the operational instrument of the STAG framework. It is packaged as a machine-readable data file and as a human-readable document. The machine-readable data file has the following structure:

For each field: field_name, field_type, permitted_values, required, required_when_applicable, description, related_rule.

For each rule: rule_number, rule_name, description, related_fields.

For each display label: label_name, label_description, derivation_rule.

For each anchoring status: status_name, status_description, conditions.

Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Main Flow (Python Binding)
function validate(stagRecord, options):

Step 1. schemaVersion = options.schemaVersion or LATEST_SCHEMA_VERSION.

Step 2. schema = schemaRegistry.getJSONSchema(schemaVersion).

Step 3. structuralViolations = jsonschema.validate(stagRecord, schema).

Step 4. shaclViolations = [].

if options.validationScope != "structural_only":

shaclSchema = schemaRegistry.getSHACLSchema(schemaVersion).

shaclViolations = pyshacl.validate(stagRecord, shaclSchema).

Step 5. semanticViolations = [].

if options.validationScope != "structural_only":

ruleSet = ruleRegistry.getRuleSet(schemaVersion).

for rule in ruleSet.rules:

result = rule(stagRecord).

if result is not PASS:

semanticViolations.push({ruleNumber: rule.number, ruleName: rule.name, severity: "error", fieldPath: result.field, offendingValue: result.value, message: result.message}).

Step 6. allViolations = structuralViolations.concat(shaclViolations).concat(semanticViolations).

Step 7. return {pass: allViolations.length == 0, violations: allViolations, schemaVersion: schemaVersion, ruleSetVersion: ruleSet.version}.

7.2 Get Field List
function getFieldList(schemaVersion):

fieldRegistry = fieldRegistry.get(schemaVersion).

return fieldRegistry.fields.

7.3 Get Permitted Values
function getPermittedValues(fieldName, schemaVersion):

fieldRegistry = fieldRegistry.get(schemaVersion).

return fieldRegistry.permittedValues[fieldName].

7.4 Get Rule List
